facts:
A connected network has an **Eulerian circuit** exactly when every vertex has an even degree.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3,0);
\coordinate (R) at (3,3);
\coordinate (S) at (0,3);
\draw (P) -- (Q);
\draw (Q) -- (R);
\draw (R) -- (S);
\draw (S) -- (P);
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P\,(2)$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q\,(2)$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R\,(2)$};
\node[above left] at (S) {$S\,(2)$};
\node at (1.5,-1.4) {no odd vertices};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A connected network with **exactly two** odd vertices has an Eulerian trail only, starting at one odd vertex and finishing at the other.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3,0);
\coordinate (R) at (3,3);
\coordinate (S) at (0,3);
\draw (P) -- (Q);
\draw (Q) -- (R);
\draw (R) -- (S);
\draw (S) -- (P);
\draw (P) -- (R);
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P\,(3)$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q\,(2)$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R\,(3)$};
\node[above left] at (S) {$S\,(2)$};
\node at (1.5,-1.4) {two odd vertices: $P$ and $R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

With **more than two** odd vertices there is neither an Eulerian trail nor an Eulerian circuit.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3,0);
\coordinate (R) at (3,3);
\coordinate (S) at (0,3);
\draw (P) -- (Q);
\draw (Q) -- (R);
\draw (R) -- (S);
\draw (S) -- (P);
\draw (P) -- (R);
\draw (Q) -- (S);
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P\,(3)$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q\,(3)$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R\,(3)$};
\node[above left] at (S) {$S\,(3)$};
\node at (1.5,-1.4) {four odd vertices};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

