Every vertex in this network has degree $2$. Explain why there is no Eulerian circuit covering the whole network. If extra edges may be added, including separate edges between the same pair of vertices, find the smallest number needed to permit such a circuit and show where they could go.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (J) at (0,0);
\coordinate (K) at (2,0);
\coordinate (L) at (1,1.8);
\coordinate (M) at (4,0);
\coordinate (N) at (6,0);
\coordinate (P) at (5,1.8);
\draw (J)--(K)--(L)--(J);
\draw (M)--(N)--(P)--(M);
\foreach \v in {J,K,L,M,N,P}{\fill (\v) circle (2pt);}
\path (J) node[below left] {$J$} (K) node[below] {$K$} (L) node[above] {$L$} (M) node[below] {$M$} (N) node[below right] {$N$} (P) node[above] {$P$};
